From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:15:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: qseecom: notify TrustZone of the app region

qcom_scm_qseecom_app_load() fails every trustlet load with -ENOMEM,
remapped from the raw SMC error QCOM_SCM_ENOMEM: TrustZone refuses at
the transport level, before an app-manager result is ever produced.
The image itself is fine -- correctly sized, correctly laid out, under
the 4 GB line the loader already checks for.

The vendor driver sends QSEOS_APP_REGION_NOTIFICATION at probe and
fails probe if it does not succeed, handing TrustZone the physical
address and size of the memory region app images may be loaded into.
Some platforms have this done by the bootloader before Linux runs, and
say so via the DT property qcom,appsbl-qseecom-support, which the
vendor driver takes as license to skip the call itself. But that
property only means the bootloader is *expected* to have done it -- on
a boot path that never runs the Android flows QSEE was designed around
(i.e. any mainline boot), nothing guarantees it actually did. When it
did not, TrustZone has no app-loadable region configured at all, and
QSEOS_APP_START has nowhere to put the image -- which is exactly the
-ENOMEM observed.

Add qcom_scm_qseecom_app_region_notify(). Unlike the neighbouring
qseecom calls, the region address and size are not carried through a
request buffer: the vendor driver's own dispatch for this command
(qseecom.c, the QSEOS_APP_REGION_NOTIFICATION case) sets desc.args[0]
and desc.args[1] directly from the address and size it was given, and
never hands TrustZone a pointer to anything -- its "ireq" structs for
this command exist only to carry those two values through one C switch
statement, and QSEE's own internal command tag for this operation
(0x0D, counted from the vendor's qseecom_qceos_cmd_id enum) is never
sent either, since the SMC id already encodes the operation. So this
call is just desc.args[0]/[1] = addr/size and a check of the result --
no tzmem allocation.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h |  6 +++
 2 files changed, 66 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 535a12e252c0..ef0051814e09 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ enum qcom_scm_qseecom_tz_svc {
 enum qcom_scm_qseecom_tz_cmd_app {
 	QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_APP_SEND			= 1,
 	QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_APP_LOOKUP		= 3,
+	QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_APP_REGION_NOTIFICATION	= 5,
 	/*
 	 * The command space is per (owner, svc): APP_SEND is
 	 * (TZ_APPS, APP_ID_PLACEHOLDER) and APP_START is (QSEE_OS, APP_MGR),
@@ -2330,6 +2331,65 @@ static int qcom_scm_qseecom_check_dma32(phys_addr_t phys, size_t size)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/**
+ * qcom_scm_qseecom_app_region_notify() - Tell TrustZone where the QSEE app
+ * memory region is.
+ * @addr: Physical base address of the region reserved for QSEE app images.
+ * @size: Size of the region, in bytes.
+ *
+ * On some platforms the bootloader hands QSEE this region before Linux ever
+ * runs; on others (advertised to the vendor driver via the DT property
+ * "qcom,appsbl-qseecom-support", which makes it skip issuing this call from
+ * its own probe) that hand-off is only assumed to have happened, and does
+ * not necessarily happen on a boot path that never runs the OS flows QSEE
+ * expects. When QSEE has no app-loadable region configured at all,
+ * QSEOS_APP_START fails at the SCM transport layer with QCOM_SCM_ENOMEM
+ * (surfacing as -ENOMEM), before any app-manager result is ever produced,
+ * simply because there is nowhere to place the app image.
+ *
+ * This call is the fix for that: it must be issued once, before the first
+ * qcom_scm_qseecom_app_load(), on any platform where nothing else has
+ * already told TrustZone about the region. The vendor driver treats a
+ * failure here as fatal to its own probe.
+ *
+ * Unlike the neighbouring qseecom calls, @addr and @size are passed to
+ * TrustZone as plain scalar arguments, not through a request buffer: the
+ * vendor driver's own dispatch for this command (qseecom.c, the
+ * QSEOS_APP_REGION_NOTIFICATION case) sets desc.args[0]/[1] directly from
+ * the region address and size it was given, and never hands TrustZone a
+ * pointer to anything. The vendor's "ireq" structs for this command exist
+ * only to carry those two values through that one C switch statement; nothing
+ * in the vendor tree ever copies one into TZ-visible memory. QSEE's own
+ * command tag (QSEOS_APP_REGION_NOTIFICATION, counted as 0x0D from the
+ * vendor's qseecom_qceos_cmd_id enum) is likewise never sent -- the SMC id
+ * already encodes the operation.
+ *
+ * Return: Zero on success, nonzero on failure.
+ */
+int qcom_scm_qseecom_app_region_notify(phys_addr_t addr, size_t size)
+{
+	struct qcom_scm_desc desc = {};
+	struct qcom_scm_qseecom_resp res = {};
+	int status;
+
+	desc.owner = QSEECOM_TZ_OWNER_QSEE_OS;
+	desc.svc = QSEECOM_TZ_SVC_APP_MGR;
+	desc.cmd = QSEECOM_TZ_CMD_APP_REGION_NOTIFICATION;
+	desc.arginfo = QCOM_SCM_ARGS(2, QCOM_SCM_RW, QCOM_SCM_VAL);
+	desc.args[0] = addr;
+	desc.args[1] = size;
+
+	status = qcom_scm_qseecom_call(&desc, &res);
+	if (status)
+		return status;
+
+	if (res.result != QSEECOM_RESULT_SUCCESS)
+		return -EIO;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qcom_scm_qseecom_app_region_notify);
+
 /**
  * qcom_scm_qseecom_app_load() - Load a QSEE app from its MDT image.
  * @app_name: The name of the app, as the TZ knows it.
diff --git a/include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h b/include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h
index f0006a098c43..da3099bcbee6 100644
--- a/include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h
+++ b/include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h
@@ -174,6 +174,7 @@ int qcom_scm_shm_bridge_delete(u64 handle);
 #ifdef CONFIG_QCOM_QSEECOM
 
 int qcom_scm_qseecom_app_get_id(const char *app_name, u32 *app_id);
+int qcom_scm_qseecom_app_region_notify(phys_addr_t addr, size_t size);
 int qcom_scm_qseecom_app_load(const char *app_name, phys_addr_t img_phys,
 			      size_t mdt_len, size_t img_len, u32 *app_id);
 int qcom_scm_qseecom_app_send(u32 app_id, void *req, size_t req_size,
@@ -186,6 +187,11 @@ static inline int qcom_scm_qseecom_app_get_id(const char *app_name, u32 *app_id)
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
+static inline int qcom_scm_qseecom_app_region_notify(phys_addr_t addr, size_t size)
+{
+	return -EINVAL;
+}
+
 static inline int qcom_scm_qseecom_app_load(const char *app_name,
 					    phys_addr_t img_phys,
 					    size_t mdt_len, size_t img_len,
